{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/localization"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"role":"article","title":"Localization","roleHeading":"Article"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Localization","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How the default placeholders’ built-in text is localized, how to add a language, and how to show different text instead without touching ScreenStates itself."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default Empty\/Loading\/Error placeholders’ text — “Nothing Here,” “Loading,” “Retry,” “Something Went Wrong,” “Connection Issue” — comes from a String Catalog, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings"},{"type":"text","text":", resolved from ScreenStates’ own bundle ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bundle.module"},{"type":"text","text":") rather than your app’s. That’s deliberate: a custom title your app passes in (see below) is never run back through localization, and a language you add to "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"your own"}]},{"type":"text","text":" app’s catalog has no effect on these five strings — they only ever resolve against ScreenStates’ bundle. English, Spanish, French, and Russian are built in today."}]},{"anchor":"Adding-a-language-to-ScreenStates","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Adding a language to ScreenStates"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a change to the package itself, not something a consuming app can do on its own — it needs a PR. Open "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings"},{"type":"text","text":" and add a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localizations"},{"type":"text","text":" entry for the new language code under each of the five string keys:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"json","code":["\"Retry\" : {","  \"comment\" : \"Title of the button that retries loading after an error.\",","  \"localizations\" : {","    \"en\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Retry\" } },","    \"de\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Wiederholen\" } }","  }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every one of the five keys needs an entry for every language — a string present in English but missing a translation elsewhere fails CI (see below). "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStatesStrings.swift"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s doc comments list all five keys and their English text if you’re starting from scratch."}]},{"anchor":"Overriding-text-per-app","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overriding text per-app"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You don’t need a new language, or a PR, to show different text than the built-in default — two options, depending on how much you want to replace:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title:)"},{"type":"text","text":" takes a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"title"},{"type":"text","text":" directly, bypassing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Localizable.xcstrings"},{"type":"text","text":" entirely for that one string. Pass your own localized string (from your own app’s String Catalog, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSLocalizedString"},{"type":"text","text":", whatever) instead of the default:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title: String(localized: \"No Results\"))"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultErrorView"},{"type":"text","text":" has no equivalent for its title or Retry button text today — only the error’s own message is customizable, via "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For anything else — the Error placeholder’s title, the Retry button’s text, or any text at all in a shape the built-in views don’t expose a parameter for — pass a fully custom placeholder instead of the default one, via "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"empty"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loading"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error"},{"type":"text","text":" builder closures (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") or "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateViewController","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"‘s equivalent. A custom placeholder can still reuse "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" so VoiceOver announces transitions with the same wording your custom text uses, instead of the default’s."}]}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateStore"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","title":"ScreenStateStore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" holder of a screen’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", driving both"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI and UIKit consumers from a single source of truth."}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateStore"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore","type":"topic"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateContainerView":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateContainerView"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView","title":"ScreenStateContainerView","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIView"},{"type":"text","text":" that swaps its content for the right placeholder based on a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", mirroring "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" from the SwiftUI side."}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateContainerView"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatecontainerview","type":"topic"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/GettingStartedWithUIKit":{"abstract":[{"text":"Drive a UIKit screen’s four states with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","kind":"article","role":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/gettingstartedwithuikit","title":"Getting Started with UIKit"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateDisplayableError":{"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenStateDisplayableError","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","title":"ScreenStateDisplayableError","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Lets an error type supply its own user-facing message, distinct from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localizedDescription"},{"type":"text","text":" — which is often a debugging string (or, for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"type":"text","text":" with no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomStringConvertible"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocalizedError"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conformance, just the type name) rather than something to put in front"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the person using the app."}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenStateDisplayableError","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatedisplayableerror","type":"topic"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateView":{"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstateview","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"ScreenStateView","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateView"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateView"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Renders the right content for a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", switching between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Empty \/ Loading \/ Data \/ Error automatically."}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates":{"kind":"symbol","title":"ScreenStates","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give any screen a standard "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Empty"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Loading"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"type":"text","text":" state, usable from both UIKit and SwiftUI."}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI":{"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/gettingstartedwithswiftui","title":"Getting Started with SwiftUI","type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","abstract":[{"text":"Drive a SwiftUI screen’s four states with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/Accessibility":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility","title":"Accessibility","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything the default placeholders — and your own custom ones — get for free: VoiceOver, Reduce Motion, Increase Contrast, Dynamic Type, and stable identifiers for XCUITest."}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/accessibility","type":"topic"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateViewController":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenStateViewController","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateViewController","title":"ScreenStateViewController","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIViewController"},{"type":"text","text":" base class that owns a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pinned to the view’s edges and bound to a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wrapping the boilerplate every UIKit screen using ScreenStates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"otherwise repeats in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"viewDidLoad()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenStateViewController","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstateviewcontroller","type":"topic"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenState/accessibilityAnnouncement":{"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"accessibilityAnnouncement","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement","title":"accessibilityAnnouncement","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The same text the default placeholders announce to VoiceOver for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this case, reusable by a fully custom placeholder that wants to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"announce transitions with the same wording instead of inventing its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":", since at that point a custom placeholder’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own content is what VoiceOver should read, not a transition"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"announcement."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstate\/accessibilityannouncement","type":"topic"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenState":{"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstate","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"ScreenState","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenState"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenState"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The four canonical states of a screen: nothing to show yet, in flight,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"showing data, or failed."}]}}}